      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-252748",
      ":question/problem": "A school director surveyed $16$ students, asking them if they were satisfied with their extracurricular activities. The sample includes students attending either sports or music activities. The director wants to determine if students' satisfaction and activity type are independent.\n\nThe following contingency table reports the frequency distribution of the sample.\n\nFill in the missing values of the expected frequencies under the hypothesis that the features are independent.\n\n|  | Sport | Music |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Not Satisfied | $O_{11} = 2$<br>$E_{11} =$ {{field-1}} | $O_{12} = 6$<br>$E_{12} =$ {{field-2}} |\n| Satisfied | $O_{21} = 7$<br>$E_{21} =$ {{field-3}} | $O_{22} = 1$<br>$E_{22} =$ {{field-4}} |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    }
